<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle by Tauri. Keys live here rather than in Rust because none of them is a
  platform *seam* — `src-tauri/tests/platform_seams.rs` caps `#[cfg(target_os)]` at two files, and
  this costs nothing against that budget.

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription. macOS attributes a child process's microphone access to the
  responsible application, so this is what produces the prompt when SoX runs. Claude Code ships a
  whole helper .app for the same reason: a bare CLI binary has no bundle to put this in. wtm already
  is one.

  A signed release needs one more thing: the hardened runtime denies the microphone without even
  this prompt unless the app also carries `com.apple.security.device.audio-input`, which
  Entitlements.plist supplies.

  Known rough edge, documented in the README rather than hidden: a local build is signed ad-hoc, so
  its TCC grant is keyed to a signature that changes on every rebuild — the prompt comes back after
  `just build`. A release's Developer ID signature does not change, so its grant survives updates.

  NSUserNotificationAlertStyle. wtm notifies only while it is in the background, and only when a
  session is waiting on you or has stopped, so the notification is the one thing that brings you
  back. macOS's default style is a banner that slides away after a few seconds into Notification
  Center, which means it is gone by the time you look. "alert" stays on screen until it is
  answered. It only chooses the starting style for an app macOS has not seen before: the switch in
  System Settings → Notifications is the user's, and an install that already exists keeps the
  setting it has.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>wtm records your voice only while you hold the dictation button in a prompt composer, and sends that recording to Deepgram to be turned into text.</string>
  <key>NSUserNotificationAlertStyle</key>
  <string>alert</string>
</dict>
</plist>
